THE ONE HAND-BUILT WORKAROUND -- READ THIS, IT IS THE REAL FINDING
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This gate CANNOT be crossed by the documented flow alone. Magic has no `device`
line for an inductor in sky130A.tech, so a drawn spiral extracts as plain wire and
both coil terminals land on ONE node:
    Ports "B" and "A" are electrically shorted
and the short PROPAGATES: `equiv "B" "A"` in vco_spiral_ind.ext collapses
VDD + voutp + voutn into a single net, and the top cell extracts with 4 ports.

Levers that DO NOT work (established by the pre-shortening run, not re-tested here
because the coil cell is bit-for-bit unchanged -- verified: 347 polygons, identical
layer histogram, identical 2 labels, identical bbox):
  - `ignore class "-circuit1/2 vco_spiral_ind"` alone: insufficient. Those lines can
    only delete a subcircuit INSTANCE, and there is none on the layout side because
    ext2spice omits a subcircuit containing no devices. The damage happens inside
    Magic, upstream of anything netgen can be told.
  - `property LEFview true`: FAILS SILENTLY. Magic 8.3 accepts it with no error and
    extracts the coil internals anyway.
  - editing the .ext to delete the `equiv`: recovers voutn but not voutp -- the
    parent's hierarchical merges were already written against the merged canonical
    node, and splitting a child cannot undo a parent assignment.

What DOES work, and what I rebuilt against the NEW geometry (the recipe is
re-applied, not reused -- the shortened GDS is a different file):
  an EXTRACTION-ONLY GDS view, layout_fixer_work/regate/lvs_attempt_1/routed_lvsview.gds
    - deleted the ONE 74-point met5 (72/20) spiral polygon of vco_spiral_ind
      (bbox -98,-44 .. 98,153) that fuses A to B;
    - re-added an 8x5 um met5 patch (90,148)..(98,153) under port B so its pin still
      lands on real met5;
    - kept everything else: all 340 via4 (71/44) cuts, all three met4 (71/20)
      landings, the met5 port-A stub, both (72,16) labels A and B.
  Result: 0x "electrically shorted", no `equiv` line in vco_spiral_ind.ext, node A
  and node B independent, 6 ports.
  The coil is then black-boxed on BOTH sides by two lines appended to a copy of the
  stock netgen setup (sky130A_setup_vco.tcl):
      ignore class "-circuit1 vco_spiral_ind"
      ignore class "-circuit2 vco_spiral_ind"

THE DELIVERED GDS IS NOT MODIFIED. routed_lvsview.gds is a scratch copy that exists
only to be extracted. Do not ship it and do not DRC it (deleting the spiral would
of course change the circuit).

ASSESSMENT / OWNERSHIP: this is a TOOLING gap, not a layout bug, and it is not mine
to fix in geometry. It is the reason this gate is not reproducible unattended for
this circuit class: any design containing a drawn inductor will hit the same wall
and will need the same hand-built extraction view. A durable fix belongs upstream
of layout-fixer -- either a real `device` line / abstract view for the spiral cell
in the PDK's Magic tech, or a scripted "black-box this cell for extraction" step
that builds the view automatically from the primitive's port list. Flagged to the
orchestrator.

